# SABOTAGE: T160 (spec §I4 completion) — flips `Samen.CRM.AccountLink.domain_match/2`'s
# exhaustive `[one] -> match | _ -> no-match` pattern to `[one | _] -> match | [] -> no-
# match`. Two or more CONFIDENT domain candidates (a genuinely ambiguous match — e.g. two
# billing customers both use the shared brokerage's domain) now silently resolves to
# WHICHEVER candidate the underlying read happened to return FIRST — an unstable guess,
# not the honest "cannot resolve confidently" absence the fail-closed contract promises
# (mirrors T74 `Samen.Mailbox.Match`'s own "an ambiguous match is never resolved by
# guessing" discipline). A company's MRR/health could flip between TWO real customers'
# numbers depending on read ordering — never a stable, honest answer either way. Reverts
# byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_account_health_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: T160 FAIL-CLOSED AMBIGUOUS: TWO customers share the same domain -> honest no-match, never a guess
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
@@ -164,8 +164,8 @@
     # FAIL-CLOSED: exactly one confident candidate resolves; zero OR two-or-more
     # (ambiguous — never guessed) both resolve to honest absence.
     case matches do
-      [one] -> {:ok, one, :domain}
-      _ -> {:error, :not_linked}
+      [one | _] -> {:ok, one, :domain}
+      [] -> {:error, :not_linked}
     end
   rescue
     _ -> {:error, :not_linked}
